<title>USA: MBIA files shelf for $250 mln in debt/stock.</title>
<headline>MBIA files shelf for $250 mln in debt/stock.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Inc said Tuesday it filed a shelf registration with the Securities and Exchange Commission to sell up to $250 million in debt securities and preferred and common shares.</p>
<p>Proceeds will be used to provide additional capital for the future needs of the company and MBIA Corp and general corporate purposes, the filing said.</p>
<p>MBIA Inc, of Armonk, New York, insures municipal bonds, asset-backed securities and other non-municipal bonds through its wholly-owned subsidiary, MBIA Insurance Corp.</p>
</text>
